WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.680
With Maze Runner: The Scorch Trials out now,
let's take a look at 7 things you probably

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.959
didn't know about the big-screen adaptation
of James Dashner's best-selling novel.

00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:16.500
According to the cast, The Scorch Trials was
even more physically demanding and involved

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.490
even more running than the first movie.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:23.470
So, when Ki Hong Lee, who plays Minho, was
running up sand dunes, he suffered a minor

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.189
fracture to one of his knees.

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:28.029
But that wasn't the only injury he sustained
on set.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:32.090
He also cut himself several times after he
asked for a real knife instead of using a

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.640
blunt one for a scene where he flipped a knife
and caught it.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.090
As for Kaya Scodelario, who plays Teresa,
although she avoided injury while filming

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.840
The Maze Runner, she wasn't so lucky on The
Scorch Trials where she had back and knee

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.520
problems from all the running.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.550
And being barefoot for part of the movie proved
its own hazard as Scodelario ran into a bolt

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:56.710
sticking that was up out of the set floor
and pulled off her toenail!

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.070
The main cast took part in a boot camp before
The Scorch Trials began filming.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:05.790
However, whereas training for the first movie
included learning survival skills and camping

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:10.390
overnight in the wooded Louisiana location
used for the Glade, The Scorch Trials boot

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:16.250
camp involved running 2 to 3 miles a day in
Albuquerque's mile-high altitude and practising

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.280
stunts such as a long slide through a closing
door and a leap-into-mid-air-kick.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:27.119
Most of the movie's sand dune scenes were
filmed at Pajarito Dunes, west of Albuquerque

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.369
in New Mexico.

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:33.200
The design team removed footprints and vehicle
tracks from the dunes by sweeping with rakes

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:40.549
and used a low-hovering helicopter as a giant
fan to create a swirling effect in the sand.

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:44.570
After a hard day filming The Scorch Trials,
many of the cast spent the evenings hanging

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.219
out together, playing Mario Kart and cooking.

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:51.899
Kaya Scodelario made Brazilian dishes and
reckoned she was the best in the kitchen because

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:54.670
she's inherited her Brazilian mother's cooking
gene.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:58.990
Dylan O'Brien's specialities were chicken
parmesan and breaded chicken cutlets, while

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:04.250
Dexter Darden, who plays Frypan, loved to
grill and also made a mean macaroni and cheese

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:07.360
as well as fried chicken.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:13.380
The movie's party sequence was shot over two
days at an 8,500-square-foot mansion known

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.870
as The Castle in downtown Albuquerque.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:21.080
The Castle was built over two years from 2006
and was the home of late jewellery designer

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.080
Gertrude Zachary.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:27.400
During filming, the walls of the mansion were
covered in dark green wallpaper aged with

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:32.620
mildew and staining to give this quite new
building the feel of a grand mansion past

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.980
its glory days.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:39.940
The design team also added hundreds of candles
melted down into mounds, and VHS tape that

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.910
was pulled out to use as streamers.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:49.060
The dark tunnels, storm drains and diversion
channels under the University of New Mexico

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.440
Hospital in Albuquerque proved the perfect
place to film scenes set beneath the desolate

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.750
landscape of the Scorch.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:02.630
The sequences in Jorge's lair were filmed
on sets constructed at Albuquerque Studios

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:07.860
and at the vacant railyard complex south of
downtown Albuquerque, where movies including

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:13.110
The Avengers and Terminator: Salvation, and
TV show Breaking Bad have also filmed.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:17.860
The design of where the scavengers live in
the lair was inspired by the look of Kowloon

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:22.920
Walled City in Hong Kong, a now-demolished
stacked building structure where people lived

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.840
in very cramped conditions.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.720
Lots of the objects used to dress the set
of Jorge's penthouse were bits of metal and

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.740
junk furniture found in salvage and recycling
yards.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:37.390
Now, let me know in the comments below, who's
your favourite character in The Maze Runner

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:38.390
series?

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:41.470
And what's your favourite book-to-big-screen
adaptation &amp; why?

